{"version":19,"type":"full","exportedAt":1793146333806,"world":{"id":"p5RB-gewXUZYlHUKTH5pw","name":"What the Dark Is Owed","description":"A gritty space opera in three eras. Lantern, a hollow-rock habitat beyond the Throat, keeps its air on credit: every breath is owed. Across seven centuries — the Closing, the Owing and the Healing — three sets of strangers fight the same debt.","coverImageId":null,"theme":"theme-scifi","continuityStaleThreshold":5,"calendar":{"week":{"days":["Monday","Tuesday","Wednesday","Thursday","Friday","Saturday","Sunday"],"first":3},"leap":{"month":1,"days":1,"every":4,"skip":100,"keep":400},"startYear":2387,"yearSuffix":"CE","months":[{"name":"January","days":31},{"name":"February","days":28},{"name":"March","days":31},{"name":"April","days":30},{"name":"May","days":31},{"name":"June","days":30},{"name":"July","days":31},{"name":"August","days":31},{"name":"September","days":30},{"name":"October","days":31},{"name":"November","days":30},{"name":"December","days":31}],"eras":[{"label":"CE","counts":"up","first":1},{"label":"AC","start":2388,"counts":"up","first":1}]},"pinsSetClock":true,"createdAt":1793144674147,"updatedAt":1793144906847},"mapLayers":[],"locationMarkers":[{"id":"0nvafHfyRK1XBFvbSx62k","worldId":"p5RB-gewXUZYlHUKTH5pw","mapLayerId":null,"linkedMapLayerId":null,"name":"The Pumphouse","description":"Lantern's air plant and water stills, deep in the fore wall. Every scrubber and valve is keyed to the Tally.","x":0,"y":0,"imageId":null,"iconType":"building","tags":[],"factionId":null,"createdAt":1793145067327,"updatedAt":1793145067327,"version":1},{"id":"22kcZBjgWU3tyDAJK5eLn","worldId":"p5RB-gewXUZYlHUKTH5pw","mapLayerId":null,"linkedMapLayerId":null,"name":"Caul Deep","description":"The Company's deep ice mine on Caul. Shut down in the spring of 2387.","x":0,"y":0,"imageId":null,"iconType":"dungeon","tags":[],"factionId":null,"createdAt":1793145080142,"updatedAt":1793145080142,"version":1},{"id":"6WhnhSdLptwpOg_y6XG7V","worldId":"p5RB-gewXUZYlHUKTH5pw","mapLayerId":null,"linkedMapLayerId":null,"name":"The Covenant","description":"The Halden-Ash Company's last ship in the Sabra system, a long-haul carrier docked at Lantern's fore lock.","x":0,"y":0,"imageId":null,"iconType":"building","tags":[],"factionId":null,"createdAt":1793145086545,"updatedAt":1793145086545,"version":1},{"id":"AHMcYZIInNNvfUZfIUJri","worldId":"p5RB-gewXUZYlHUKTH5pw","mapLayerId":null,"linkedMapLayerId":null,"name":"Nhai","description":"The gas giant Lantern orbits. Banded ochre and bruise-purple, with a thin ring.","x":0,"y":0,"imageId":null,"iconType":"region","tags":[],"factionId":null,"createdAt":1793145084409,"updatedAt":1793145084409,"version":1},{"id":"GS98RIEmER9V5IIOiC590","worldId":"p5RB-gewXUZYlHUKTH5pw","mapLayerId":null,"linkedMapLayerId":null,"name":"Throat-Watch Station","description":"The Company's monitoring station near the Throat, which measures the wormhole's breathing.","x":0,"y":0,"imageId":null,"iconType":"building","tags":[],"factionId":null,"createdAt":1793145090824,"updatedAt":1793145090824,"version":1},{"id":"Ioi0lAWzNGfKuD6sO0y_s","worldId":"p5RB-gewXUZYlHUKTH5pw","mapLayerId":null,"linkedMapLayerId":null,"name":"Lantern","description":"A hollowed nickel-iron asteroid in orbit of the gas giant Nhai, spun for gravity, eleven kilometres long. Built by the Halden-Ash Company as the Sabra Concern's habitat. Lit from within by the Wick.","x":0,"y":0,"imageId":null,"iconType":"city","tags":[],"factionId":null,"createdAt":1793145056640,"updatedAt":1793145056640,"version":1},{"id":"LYsa4T85OiMWSOVa_8uQa","worldId":"p5RB-gewXUZYlHUKTH5pw","mapLayerId":null,"linkedMapLayerId":null,"name":"The Wick","description":"The fusion lamp that runs down Lantern's axis like a candle-wick: the habitat's sun. Tended from catwalks and crawls along the spine. Fed by fuel cassettes.","x":0,"y":0,"imageId":null,"iconType":"landmark","tags":[],"factionId":null,"createdAt":1793145058767,"updatedAt":1793145058767,"version":1},{"id":"Q5Iq2IntJfkK2QbC7YeH_","worldId":"p5RB-gewXUZYlHUKTH5pw","mapLayerId":null,"linkedMapLayerId":null,"name":"The Good Title","description":"A Throat-runner ship out of Port Ambry, mortgaged to Brightwater Recovery, captained by Mabry Ode.","x":0,"y":0,"imageId":null,"iconType":"building","tags":[],"factionId":null,"createdAt":1793145095120,"updatedAt":1793145095120,"version":1},{"id":"RgGiohTxgEkbv_a0TO0in","worldId":"p5RB-gewXUZYlHUKTH5pw","mapLayerId":null,"linkedMapLayerId":null,"name":"The Magpie","description":"Kas Ostrova's ice hauler: a battered tug with a tank-frame, on the Caul run.","x":0,"y":0,"imageId":null,"iconType":"building","tags":[],"factionId":null,"createdAt":1793145088692,"updatedAt":1793145088692,"version":1},{"id":"Ybosum8zedJ0zQI6eapQp","worldId":"p5RB-gewXUZYlHUKTH5pw","mapLayerId":null,"linkedMapLayerId":null,"name":"Port Ambry","description":"Concord frontier station on the far side of the Throat, built when the Throat was dead, waiting seven hundred years for it to heal.","x":0,"y":0,"imageId":null,"iconType":"city","tags":[],"factionId":null,"createdAt":1793145092993,"updatedAt":1793145092993,"version":1},{"id":"ZXX5Bvu5ikNR9QVw8Xe3x","worldId":"p5RB-gewXUZYlHUKTH5pw","mapLayerId":null,"linkedMapLayerId":null,"name":"The Upper Wards","description":"The best-lit terraces near Lantern's fore end, nearest the Counting House. Company staff housing in 2387; the counting families' quarter in the Owing.","x":0,"y":0,"imageId":null,"iconType":"town","tags":[],"factionId":null,"createdAt":1793145069455,"updatedAt":1793145069455,"version":1},{"id":"b2s6PBgzitLmRSeQ38clE","worldId":"p5RB-gewXUZYlHUKTH5pw","mapLayerId":null,"linkedMapLayerId":null,"name":"The Salt Docks","description":"The old ice docks at the aft end of the Dock Ring, half-abandoned, where the Salt land ice run off Caul outside the Tally.","x":0,"y":0,"imageId":null,"iconType":"town","tags":[],"factionId":null,"createdAt":1793145075859,"updatedAt":1793145075859,"version":1},{"id":"bpyo3ZRm53_YW7_EkVCbh","worldId":"p5RB-gewXUZYlHUKTH5pw","mapLayerId":null,"linkedMapLayerId":null,"name":"The Dock Ring","description":"Lantern's docking ring at the fore end of the rock, where the haulers come in from Caul. The Ardent Mercy's bell hangs at the inner lock, on the Bell Hook.","x":0,"y":0,"imageId":null,"iconType":"building","tags":[],"factionId":null,"createdAt":1793145063051,"updatedAt":1793145063051,"version":1},{"id":"fNC0HTz6yaBkVBuz8tMlw","worldId":"p5RB-gewXUZYlHUKTH5pw","mapLayerId":null,"linkedMapLayerId":null,"name":"The Throat","description":"The wormhole at the edge of the Sabra system, Lantern's only road to the Concord.","x":0,"y":0,"imageId":null,"iconType":"landmark","tags":[],"factionId":null,"createdAt":1793145082272,"updatedAt":1793145082272,"version":1},{"id":"fc68DOqhWtybQVCIoXxgn","worldId":"p5RB-gewXUZYlHUKTH5pw","mapLayerId":null,"linkedMapLayerId":null,"name":"Caul","description":"Nhai's ice moon. Lantern's water comes from it.","x":0,"y":0,"imageId":null,"iconType":"region","tags":[],"factionId":null,"createdAt":1793145078002,"updatedAt":1793145078002,"version":1},{"id":"jWi-Bx-VXJvuRZ3e3EWY5","worldId":"p5RB-gewXUZYlHUKTH5pw","mapLayerId":null,"linkedMapLayerId":null,"name":"The Counting House","description":"The vault at Lantern's core where the Tally engine runs, with the Company's offices above it. In the Owing it is the seat of the Count, built over the Hulk.","x":0,"y":0,"imageId":null,"iconType":"building","tags":[],"factionId":null,"createdAt":1793145065184,"updatedAt":1793145065184,"version":1},{"id":"nLnTyF9LPg8JbdZMm0i3Z","worldId":"p5RB-gewXUZYlHUKTH5pw","mapLayerId":null,"linkedMapLayerId":null,"name":"The Cold Wards","description":"Lantern's aft sections, abandoned, unheated and unlit: frozen streets, frost on the walls, and the dead of earlier centuries. Cutters strip them for metal.","x":0,"y":0,"imageId":null,"iconType":"dungeon","tags":[],"factionId":null,"createdAt":1793145071593,"updatedAt":1793145071593,"version":1},{"id":"obQHtZrWX1AjVLoialGbh","worldId":"p5RB-gewXUZYlHUKTH5pw","mapLayerId":null,"linkedMapLayerId":null,"name":"The Galleries","description":"The terraced housing rings carved into Lantern's inner wall, where the indentured live: bunk-rooms, chit-shops, pump galleries.","x":0,"y":0,"imageId":null,"iconType":"town","tags":[],"factionId":null,"createdAt":1793145060926,"updatedAt":1793145060926,"version":1},{"id":"pf2hnlYKmBENK4njkw23Q","worldId":"p5RB-gewXUZYlHUKTH5pw","mapLayerId":null,"linkedMapLayerId":null,"name":"The Hulk","description":"A ship-shaped mass embedded in the rock under the Counting House since the Closing. The Owing believe it is the Ardent Mercy, the ship that brought the first families.","x":0,"y":0,"imageId":null,"iconType":"building","tags":[],"factionId":null,"createdAt":1793145073723,"updatedAt":1793145073723,"version":1}],"characters":[{"id":"4DB-SYsFxGhwQg_T_P6Tr","worldId":"p5RB-gewXUZYlHUKTH5pw","name":"Wenna Blackwood","aliases":[],"description":"The Owing, 311 AC. Boss of the Salt, the smugglers who run ice off Caul outside the Tally. Sixty, one eye, a voice like a gravel chute.","portraitImageId":null,"tags":[],"isAlive":true,"color":null,"birthDate":null,"version":1,"createdAt":1793144983312,"updatedAt":1793144983312},{"id":"4PJK2irFlLq0lPkroCgPG","worldId":"p5RB-gewXUZYlHUKTH5pw","name":"Teodor Basu","aliases":[],"description":"The Closing, 2387. Comptroller of the Halden-Ash Sabra Concern. Fifty-two, precise, soft-spoken, a stammer that comes out under pressure. He designed the Tally that keys Lantern's air to its debt, and he has done something worse.","portraitImageId":null,"tags":[],"isAlive":true,"color":null,"birthDate":null,"version":1,"createdAt":1793144968427,"updatedAt":1793144968427},{"id":"8FkLsgdUH52stzy3qThJO","worldId":"p5RB-gewXUZYlHUKTH5pw","name":"Tamsin Hask","aliases":[],"description":"The Owing, 311 AC. A cutter: salvage diver in the frozen, unlit Cold Wards, stripping copper and steel from dead sections. Twenty-four, hard, funny when she forgets not to be. Born owing, like everybody.","portraitImageId":null,"tags":[],"isAlive":true,"color":null,"birthDate":null,"version":1,"createdAt":1793144976526,"updatedAt":1793144976526},{"id":"B5N-ORRxzDAoRSjwt4RPw","worldId":"p5RB-gewXUZYlHUKTH5pw","name":"Ruth Achterberg","aliases":[],"description":"The Closing, 2387. Director of the Halden-Ash Company's Sabra Concern. Sixty. Not cruel for pleasure: she counts. Wears the Director's seal, a brass key-disk, on a chain at her throat.","portraitImageId":null,"tags":[],"isAlive":true,"color":null,"birthDate":null,"version":1,"createdAt":1793144969746,"updatedAt":1793144969746},{"id":"CaEdi_nGwv_Yo9J6gmQoC","worldId":"p5RB-gewXUZYlHUKTH5pw","name":"Kas Ostrova","aliases":[],"description":"The Closing, 2387. Kasimir, Dagny's younger brother. Ice-hauler pilot on the Caul run, master of the battered hauler Magpie. Gambler, charmer, owes everybody. Loves his sister and nephew more than he can afford to.","portraitImageId":null,"tags":[],"isAlive":true,"color":null,"birthDate":null,"version":1,"createdAt":1793144967080,"updatedAt":1793144967080},{"id":"CqIecEeYy-V9MMzz8K9l0","worldId":"p5RB-gewXUZYlHUKTH5pw","name":"Odile Marchbank","aliases":[],"description":"The Closing, 2387. Dockmaster of the Dock Ring and keeper of the Ardent Mercy's bell. Seventies, half-deaf, steady engraver's hands. Rings the bell for every death on Lantern and cuts the name into the bronze.","portraitImageId":null,"tags":[],"isAlive":true,"color":null,"birthDate":null,"version":1,"createdAt":1793144972429,"updatedAt":1793144972429},{"id":"DdyKkgZFy6btLNqFcDspr","worldId":"p5RB-gewXUZYlHUKTH5pw","name":"Orrin Sallow","aliases":[],"description":"The Owing, 311 AC. A junior counter of the Counting House. Twenty-six, born in the Upper Wards to a minor counting family, believer in the Account's righteousness until he checks its arithmetic.","portraitImageId":null,"tags":[],"isAlive":true,"color":null,"birthDate":null,"version":1,"createdAt":1793144980569,"updatedAt":1793144980569},{"id":"EEp34P_LIwiHnQUS72F_S","worldId":"p5RB-gewXUZYlHUKTH5pw","name":"Corvin Saal","aliases":[],"description":"The Healing, 3089 CE. Lien adjuster for Brightwater Recovery, bonded to the firm since he was nine for his father's water debt. Forty-four. Good at his job, which is making people pay.","portraitImageId":null,"tags":[],"isAlive":true,"color":null,"birthDate":null,"version":1,"createdAt":1793144987343,"updatedAt":1793144987343},{"id":"K2sa5OCdLdT81u7a1yBt0","worldId":"p5RB-gewXUZYlHUKTH5pw","name":"Imre Vosk","aliases":[],"description":"The Owing, 311 AC. Comptroller-General of the Count, the Counting House's ruling body. Soft voice, perfect manners, holds the Count key and the lists.","portraitImageId":null,"tags":[],"isAlive":true,"color":null,"birthDate":null,"version":1,"createdAt":1793144981954,"updatedAt":1793144981954},{"id":"L41M_slYybVBTVVnpviK7","worldId":"p5RB-gewXUZYlHUKTH5pw","name":"Fen Adaire","aliases":[],"description":"The Healing, 3089 CE. Provenance archivist; she reads old corporate records for a living. Twenty-nine. Owns, by family inheritance, a bronze ship's bell inscribed ARDENT MERCY, and wants to take it home to wherever home was.","portraitImageId":null,"tags":[],"isAlive":true,"color":null,"birthDate":null,"version":1,"createdAt":1793144988698,"updatedAt":1793144988698},{"id":"LNs4_mqC3zge5HTKXOYFD","worldId":"p5RB-gewXUZYlHUKTH5pw","name":"Jory Hask","aliases":[],"description":"The Owing, 311 AC. Tamsin's brother, fifteen. A runner for anyone who pays. Light fingers.","portraitImageId":null,"tags":[],"isAlive":true,"color":null,"birthDate":null,"version":1,"createdAt":1793144979214,"updatedAt":1793144979214},{"id":"MwmknvSbYe2Ci785A2xmS","worldId":"p5RB-gewXUZYlHUKTH5pw","name":"Lemuel Adeyemi","aliases":[],"description":"The Closing, 2387. A Gallery pump-fitter whose balance crosses the dimming line on the first page.","portraitImageId":null,"tags":[],"isAlive":true,"color":null,"birthDate":null,"version":1,"createdAt":1793144975157,"updatedAt":1793144975157},{"id":"OQkh-QSkbPJM5F4BWfdhS","worldId":"p5RB-gewXUZYlHUKTH5pw","name":"Idris Kell","aliases":[],"description":"The Healing, 3089 CE. Sergeant of Brightwater's bailiffs aboard the Good Title. Professional, bored, dangerous.","portraitImageId":null,"tags":[],"isAlive":true,"color":null,"birthDate":null,"version":1,"createdAt":1793144992785,"updatedAt":1793144992785},{"id":"QFvVlO7B_a1YmFMbnd84l","worldId":"p5RB-gewXUZYlHUKTH5pw","name":"Tol Brask","aliases":[],"description":"The Healing, 3089 CE. Engineer of the Good Title, Ode's man for twenty years. Talks to machines, not people.","portraitImageId":null,"tags":[],"isAlive":true,"color":null,"birthDate":null,"version":1,"createdAt":1793144994122,"updatedAt":1793144994122},{"id":"TRqcAjx0xfYg8Pc46bEt2","worldId":"p5RB-gewXUZYlHUKTH5pw","name":"Quennell Haste","aliases":[],"description":"The Healing, 3089 CE. Junior partner of Brightwater Recovery, travelling with the claim. Courteous, tireless, legally exact.","portraitImageId":null,"tags":[],"isAlive":true,"color":null,"birthDate":null,"version":1,"createdAt":1793144991462,"updatedAt":1793144991462},{"id":"U8Xy6zAdXRBSS6PGWXunZ","worldId":"p5RB-gewXUZYlHUKTH5pw","name":"Ninian","aliases":[],"description":"The Owing, 311 AC. The last master Wickwright, keeper of the dying lamp. Very old, nearly blind from the light he has spent his life tending.","portraitImageId":null,"tags":[],"isAlive":true,"color":null,"birthDate":null,"version":1,"createdAt":1793144986013,"updatedAt":1793144986013},{"id":"WQ9NeOVAbNSpDXQKkGhBO","worldId":"p5RB-gewXUZYlHUKTH5pw","name":"Hale Varga","aliases":[],"description":"The Closing, 2387. Chief of Company Security on Lantern. Ex-Concord marine, broad, scarred, loyal to his men. His squad sealed something on Caul that he has not stopped thinking about.","portraitImageId":null,"tags":[],"isAlive":true,"color":null,"birthDate":null,"version":1,"createdAt":1793144971118,"updatedAt":1793144971118},{"id":"WshcV6xq7C75QU8kONPBB","worldId":"p5RB-gewXUZYlHUKTH5pw","name":"Mabry Ode","aliases":[],"description":"The Healing, 3089 CE. Master of the Good Title. Sixty-three, gaunt, Throat-runner in her youth. Mortgaged her ship to Brightwater to make this run.","portraitImageId":null,"tags":[],"isAlive":true,"color":null,"birthDate":null,"version":1,"createdAt":1793144990078,"updatedAt":1793144990078},{"id":"X1JRrGlyZdp8QBMZ6SYZN","worldId":"p5RB-gewXUZYlHUKTH5pw","name":"Brother Lusk","aliases":[],"description":"The Owing, 311 AC. The Bailiff of the Count: Vosk's enforcer, in grey, with a docket-baton.","portraitImageId":null,"tags":[],"isAlive":true,"color":null,"birthDate":null,"version":1,"createdAt":1793144984690,"updatedAt":1793144984690},{"id":"g_pQemPTYKrSyuBXSXecB","worldId":"p5RB-gewXUZYlHUKTH5pw","name":"Joss Teague","aliases":[],"description":"The Closing, 2387. Wick crewman, Dagny's oldest friend on the spine. Big laugh, bad knees.","portraitImageId":null,"tags":[],"isAlive":true,"color":null,"birthDate":null,"version":1,"createdAt":1793144973793,"updatedAt":1793144973793},{"id":"pDwz-N1w93a6lIKumMr7p","worldId":"p5RB-gewXUZYlHUKTH5pw","name":"Senna Hask","aliases":[],"description":"The Healing, 3089 CE. Reader of the Account on Lantern, who keeps the Tally in the Counting House.","portraitImageId":null,"tags":[],"isAlive":true,"color":null,"birthDate":null,"version":1,"createdAt":1793144995526,"updatedAt":1793144995526},{"id":"qBQ4QH8OQcPou62jFFMxx","worldId":"p5RB-gewXUZYlHUKTH5pw","name":"Dagny Ostrova","aliases":[],"description":"The Closing, 2387. Wick-tender on Lantern's axial lamp and Speaker for the Wick crews. Forty-one, widowed, dry as rust, good with her hands and better with a crowd than she wants to be. Indentured since nineteen.","portraitImageId":null,"tags":[],"isAlive":true,"color":null,"birthDate":null,"version":1,"createdAt":1793144964345,"updatedAt":1793144964345},{"id":"vOBEkx7GmTDi_KO4NiWCN","worldId":"p5RB-gewXUZYlHUKTH5pw","name":"Agathe Hask","aliases":[],"description":"The Owing, 311 AC. Tamsin's mother. Former pump-hand, now dying of lung-rot. Proud. Keeps the family's chits in a tin.","portraitImageId":null,"tags":[],"isAlive":true,"color":null,"birthDate":null,"version":1,"createdAt":1793144977846,"updatedAt":1793144977846},{"id":"xBl28xa-sqvXJ5tgbrGuh","worldId":"p5RB-gewXUZYlHUKTH5pw","name":"Pim Ostrova","aliases":[],"description":"The Closing, 2387. Dagny's son, twelve. Quick, thin, collects bolts. Worships his uncle Kas.","portraitImageId":null,"tags":[],"isAlive":true,"color":null,"birthDate":null,"version":1,"createdAt":1793144965722,"updatedAt":1793144965722}],"items":[{"id":"6bdjOpq1CGsdTR3POKzFQ","imageId":null,"worldId":"p5RB-gewXUZYlHUKTH5pw","name":"The Director's Seal","description":"A brass key-disk on a chain, the Director's half of the Tally's root keys. Engraved H-A.","iconType":"","tags":[],"version":1},{"id":"CR0TfKpzJ7APygVADXPUA","imageId":null,"worldId":"p5RB-gewXUZYlHUKTH5pw","name":"The Count Key","description":"The key by which the Comptroller-General of the Count administers the Tally. Kept in the Hulk; never shown.","iconType":"","tags":[],"version":1},{"id":"J2rCe_zB9fHmaFmATwAUF","imageId":null,"worldId":"p5RB-gewXUZYlHUKTH5pw","name":"The Tally","description":"The Halden-Ash ledger engine in the Counting House vault. Every lock, pump, scrubber and still on Lantern is keyed to it. It debits each indentured person for air, water and heat and credits their labour. A balance past the line is dimmed: doors close, rations stop.","iconType":"","tags":[],"version":1},{"id":"KjeFts84ONEtTsuUC_Ytl","imageId":null,"worldId":"p5RB-gewXUZYlHUKTH5pw","name":"The Caul List","description":"Teodor's reconstruction, from payroll, of the names of the dead of Caul Deep. Paper.","iconType":"","tags":[],"version":1},{"id":"eDxCJE9t6GVv6E49wsVUt","imageId":null,"worldId":"p5RB-gewXUZYlHUKTH5pw","name":"The Comptroller's Key","description":"Teodor Basu's half of the Tally's root keys: a slip of ceramic with a cipher burned into it, worn in his shoe.","iconType":"","tags":[],"version":1},{"id":"glZuTrPiRbVvp_16fPKY9","imageId":null,"worldId":"p5RB-gewXUZYlHUKTH5pw","name":"Fuel Cassettes","description":"Fusion fuel cassettes for the Wick, each the size of a coffin. Company property.","iconType":"","tags":[],"version":1},{"id":"lx0QoDRFeCbWybrVEqv8-","imageId":null,"worldId":"p5RB-gewXUZYlHUKTH5pw","name":"Tally Chit","description":"A stamped metal token printed with a person's Tally number and balance, carried on a cord. Children get theirs at six.","iconType":"","tags":[],"version":1},{"id":"prExb-qfLBTTeQc6lJq0W","imageId":null,"worldId":"p5RB-gewXUZYlHUKTH5pw","name":"The Mercy Bell","description":"A bronze ship's bell cast for the colony ship Ardent Mercy, hung at Lantern's inner dock lock on the Bell Hook. Rung once for every death on Lantern, and the dead's name cut into it: around the lip, then the waist, then wherever there is room.","iconType":"","tags":[],"version":1}],"characterSnapshots":[{"worldId":"p5RB-gewXUZYlHUKTH5pw","characterId":"CaEdi_nGwv_Yo9J6gmQoC","eventId":"A84nmiWcv6-wINQJ3D7BS","currentLocationMarkerId":"bpyo3ZRm53_YW7_EkVCbh","currentMapLayerId":null,"id":"-UFXd6ArQYMDKJVxHV620","sortKey":1.0000000625,"createdAt":1793145335350,"updatedAt":1793145335350,"version":1},{"worldId":"p5RB-gewXUZYlHUKTH5pw","characterId":"8FkLsgdUH52stzy3qThJO","eventId":"E7gP4pT5_i7yTLiAsRdJE","currentLocationMarkerId":"obQHtZrWX1AjVLoialGbh","currentMapLayerId":null,"id":"35M-4O7SycL4lIswJUr1H","sortKey":1.999999,"createdAt":1793145782887,"updatedAt":1793145782887,"version":1},{"worldId":"p5RB-gewXUZYlHUKTH5pw","characterId":"DdyKkgZFy6btLNqFcDspr","eventId":"yOks9hrcFzL4xJijiOILK","currentLocationMarkerId":"jWi-Bx-VXJvuRZ3e3EWY5","currentMapLayerId":null,"id":"3PbAX8FbZ7W5CFBRHxbcj","sortKey":4.999996,"createdAt":1793146319815,"updatedAt":1793146319815,"version":1